% Test cases for the wheelchair seating policy (wheelchair_seating.le):
% synthetic claims, one or two per criterion of LCD L33312 and per payment
% condition of Policy Article A52505. A cushion is an accessory of a
% wheelchair base with a claim of its own (claim 2), decided by pmd.le: a
% Group 2 standard power wheelchair with a sling/solid seat (K0822 — K0823,
% the captain's chair model, would defeat every cushion) with the findings of
% pmd_cases.le's group_2_complete. Findings are the treating practitioner's
% or the Council's; a finding nobody made leaves the answer conditional. The
% queries: whether a claim is payable (the first query, so "stage" reads its
% checklist), whether it is reasonable and necessary, and what minimal
% change would make claim 1 payable. The base claim carries no order or
% delivery facts, so it is never payable here: only claim 1 is.

the target language is: prolog.

the knowledge base wheelchair seating cases includes these resources:
    wheelchair_seating,
    pmd.

the knowledge base wheelchair seating cases includes:

query pay is:
    which claim is payable.

query rn is:
    which claim is reasonable and necessary.

query stage is:
    the query fails at which section.

query flip is:
    which minimal change to the scenario makes it the case that
        claim 1 is payable.

% A complete skin protection seat cushion (E2603) file: a covered K0822
% base, a current pressure ulcer at the seating surface, the order and the
% delivery of the cushion.
scenario skin_protection_complete is:
    claim 1 is for the seat cushion.
    the HCPCS code of the seat cushion is "E2603".
    the seat cushion is an accessory of the power wheelchair.
    the seat cushion is furnished to Ann.
    the residence of Ann is private residence.
    the date of service of claim 1 is 2026-04-10.
    the medical record of Ann documents current pressure ulcer at seating contact area.
    the order for the seat cushion is dated 2026-03-20.
    the order for the seat cushion is signed by the treating practitioner.
    the order for the seat cushion includes beneficiary name.
    the order for the seat cushion includes order date.
    the order for the seat cushion includes description of the item.
    the order for the seat cushion includes quantity to be dispensed.
    the order for the seat cushion includes treating practitioner name.
    the order for the seat cushion was communicated to the supplier on 2026-03-22.
    the seat cushion was delivered on 2026-04-10.
    the supplier holds proof of delivery for the seat cushion.
    claim 2 is for the power wheelchair.
    the HCPCS code of the power wheelchair is "K0822".
    the power wheelchair is furnished to Ann.
    the finding significant mobility limitation about Ann is established, according to the treating practitioner.
    the finding walking aids insufficient about Ann is established, according to the treating practitioner.
    the finding manual wheelchair not self propellable about Ann is established, according to the treating practitioner.
    the finding scooter ruled out about Ann is established, according to the treating practitioner.
    the finding power wheelchair can be safely operated about Ann is established, according to the treating practitioner.
    the finding home accommodates power wheelchair about Ann is established, according to the supplier.
    the finding power wheelchair will significantly improve daily activities about Ann is established, according to the treating practitioner.
    the finding willing to use power wheelchair at home about Ann is established, according to the treating practitioner.
    the weight of Ann is 180 pounds.
    pay expects answers ["claim 1 is payable"].
    rn expects answers ["claim 1 is reasonable and necessary", "claim 2 is reasonable and necessary"].
    stage expects answers [].

