% A general use back cushion (E2611) with a covered Group 3 multiple power
% option chair (K0861), a base with no captain's chair model: criterion 1.
scenario general_use_no_captains_chair_model is:
    claim 1 is for the back cushion.
    the HCPCS code of the back cushion is "E2611".
    the back cushion is an accessory of the rehab chair.
    the back cushion is furnished to Fay.
    claim 2 is for the rehab chair.
    the HCPCS code of the rehab chair is "K0861".
    the rehab chair is furnished to Fay.
    the finding significant mobility limitation about Fay is established, according to the treating practitioner.
    the finding walking aids insufficient about Fay is established, according to the treating practitioner.
    the finding manual wheelchair not self propellable about Fay is established, according to the treating practitioner.
    the finding scooter ruled out about Fay is established, according to the treating practitioner.
    the finding power wheelchair can be safely operated about Fay is established, according to the treating practitioner.
    the finding home accommodates power wheelchair about Fay is established, according to the supplier.
    the finding power wheelchair will significantly improve daily activities about Fay is established, according to the treating practitioner.
    the finding willing to use power wheelchair at home about Fay is established, according to the treating practitioner.
    the finding qualifying group 3 diagnosis about Fay is established, according to the treating practitioner, because "multiple sclerosis".
    the finding multiple power option justified about Fay is established, according to the physical therapist.
    Fay had a specialty evaluation by a licensed medical professional with no financial relationship with the supplier for the rehab chair.
    a RESNA certified assistive technology professional employed by the supplier was directly involved in the selection of the rehab chair.
    the weight of Fay is 150 pounds.
    rn expects answers ["claim 1 is reasonable and necessary", "claim 2 is reasonable and necessary"].

